The film was shot in the rocky landscape around Ramanagara, a town near Bangalore in Karnataka. To make the sets more accessible for filming, the filmmakers had to build a road linking the Bangalore highway to Ramanagara. Art director Ram Yedekar built an entire township on the location. A prison set was also constructed outdoors near Rajkamal Studio in Mumbai to ensure that its natural lighting complemented that of the on-location shoots. One section of Ramanagara was dubbed " Sippy Nagar " in honor of the film's director. As of 2010, tourists passing through Ramanagara were still offered a visit to the " Sholay rocks ", where much of the film was shot.
